From: gugu-acp <gugu-acp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:02:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] gugu: a login that names no identity is not "logged
 out"

Why: `claude auth status --json` for a bearer token, `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`
(with a custom `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` or without, in the environment or in the
settings.json `env`) or `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, reads
`{loggedIn: true, authMethod: "oauth_token", apiProvider: "firstParty"}`:
logged in, no plan, no key source (checked with Claude 2.1.282). The shared
mapper fell through to `none`, so the bridge pushed "Not logged in" for an
agent that runs turns fine. Gugu reads `none` as "sign in first" and threw
away the model catalog session/new had just returned (gugu#6857).

The module already rules that an empty read is no information, never `none`
(`fromAccountInfo`); the CLI mapper now follows the same rule. Such a read
returns undefined and nothing is pushed, while a real logged-out read
(`loggedIn: false`) still pushes `none`. The probe's log line no longer
calls such a read unparseable output.

Upstream: none yet.

Drop when: upstream stops mapping a logged-in CLI read without a plan or a
key source to `none`.
